I welcome Simon!'s feedback, which I believe clears the air and
clarifies some important issues.

> So that there will be no contextual ambiguity:  I, Simon! D. Levy,
> head of PPL1, hereby state my intention not to oppose discussion of
> legal/justice issues, so long as the prefix LEGAL or JUSTICE is used.

Okay, I suggest that we settle on LEGAL as the prefix.  It's shorter!

> If it becomes clear to me that my services are no longer required
> (i.e., that the remaining PPL1 members don't care what PPL they 
> belong to), I'll step down.

I hope Simon! remains PPL1 Head.  PPL1 just got off to a bad PR start,
nothing that can't be speedily repaired.  We need a default PPL for
newbies.  It takes newbies time to soak up the concepts and ideas around
PPLs - for that period newbies are effectively locked into PPL1. 
Newbies that flame, set the record straight offensively or whatever
(including debating the basics) can bought to task.  I suspect the
occasional hyperactive, flame-baiter newbie (eg Dale Worley) would not
last long enough to figure out the PPL business and move into other
PPLs.

>> My own proposal for the inter-PPL charter is simplicity itself.
>> Anyone can file charges against anyone, but they are judged solely
>> against the defendant's PPL charter or etiquette code.  A natural
>> Schelling point I feel, although more complex solutions must be
>> possible.
> 
> One last time: I agree.

See my slightly more complex proposal I mention in reply to Geoff.  The
idea is that a List member can only raise charges that are also
compatible with _their_ PPL's charter.

